---
title: Hex frequencies
tags: tools
summary: >-
    Counts how often each byte appears in hex, and runs of the same byte repeated 2 to 5 times, such as <code class="tool-example">00 00</code>.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% from "macros/delimiter.njk" import delimiter %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>Useful for spotting patterns in data puzzles. Runs are counted wherever they start, and a longer run counts as several shorter ones: five <code class="tool-example">41</code>s are two runs of 2.</p>
    <p>Your hex can use any of the usual delimiters between bytes (spaces, hyphens, colons, commas, semicolons, new lines, \x, 0x or %), or none, and they can be mixed. The delimiter dropdown chooses how runs are written. Copy and download give the tables as tab-separated text, which pastes into a spreadsheet.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Hex frequencies", placeholder = "Example: 48 65 6c 6c 6f 00 00 00", layout = "analysis", actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Count" }]) %}
<div class="tool-field">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Delimiter"><span class="visually-hidden">Hex </span>Delimiter</label>
    {{ delimiter(filename) }}
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
